  "query_preview": "..\nIsolated thunderstorms are developing across southern Utah with\nthe risk of flash flooding remaining possible. These storms will\ncontinue to blossom this afternoon, particularly along and near\nthe terrain of central and northern Utah. Given the saturated soil\nconditions across the region it won't take as much to lead to\nflash flooding. Drier air moves into the area for Wednesday-Friday\nas a trough across the PNW and a ridge across the southern plains\ninduces a strong pressure gradient that will lead to gusty\nsouthwest winds developing across the area with daytime gusts\n45-50 mph. \n\nThese winds will stay elevated through Friday before\nmoisture starts to advect into the region from tropical storm\nMarie in the eastern Pacific. Guidance currently highlights Sunday\nas having the greatest swath of moisture across central and\nsouthwestern Utah. Details still need to be ironed out, but given\nthe state of soil moisture there will likely be an increased risk\nof flash flooding across these areas impacted by the tropical\nmoisture this weekend.",
